From: brickassembly (ISDN_Robofab)
Subject: static_solve: accept externally applied loads

BrickSim's static_solve hard-codes gravity as the only load, so it answers
"which joint is most loaded by self-weight". Bracing (master_report §3.6)
needs "which joint is most loaded by the INSERTION PRESS". BreakageInput
already carries per-part linear (J) and angular (H) impulses, so the solver
supports applied loads; only the CLI did not expose them.

    static_solve <topology.json> [--load id,fx,fy,fz[,px,py,pz]]
                                 [--torque id,tx,ty,tz]

It also emits `clutch_forces`: the per-clutch block of BreakageSolution.x,
whose first component is the clutch's axial force in newtons (a 35.6 N press
on a 4-stud joint reads 8.903, and 71.2 N reads 17.802). Previously this was
only reachable by turning on the debug dump and decoding base64 matrices out
of /tmp.

--load takes a force in newtons on the given topology part id, optionally
applied at a point in the root frame (default: the part's centre of mass, in
which case it contributes no couple). --torque takes a pure couple. Both are
repeatable. The root reaction row now balances all three force components
rather than z alone, which the original could assume because gravity is
vertical. With no flags the output is byte-identical to the original.

Apply with:  git apply ../brickassembly/patches/static_solve_applied_load.patch
Rebuild with: pixi run -- cmake --build native/.build/release --target static_solve

Upstream: github.com/intelligent-control-lab/BrickSim @ cbd5de3
